# Quorum runs with none of these set — the voice layer falls back to the
# browser's own speech engine and the header reads "simulated".
#
# Copy this file to .env.local, which is gitignored. Never commit real values.

# ── Agora Conversational AI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All four are required together. Without any one of them the route reports
# configured: false and the app stays on the simulated transport.
#
# App ID and App Certificate: console.agora.io → Projects → your project.
# Customer ID and secret: console.agora.io → RESTful API. Different pair.
AGORA_APP_ID=
AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE=
AGORA_CUSTOMER_ID=
AGORA_CUSTOMER_SECRET=

# ── There is no fifth credential, and that is the point ─────────────────────
# Every model is Agora-managed: `credential_mode: "managed"` on the asr, llm
# and tts blocks means Agora supplies the keys and bills them inside the
# $0.10/min agent task.
#
#   ASR  Deepgram nova-3, en-IN
#   LLM  OpenAI gpt-4.1-mini
#   TTS  OpenAI tts-1, one voice per interviewer
#
# So there is no LLM_API_KEY and no TTS_KEY. If you find yourself adding one,
# the panel has stopped being an Agora build. See docs/DECISIONS.md.
#
# Note: `ares` is on Agora's published managed-vendor list but this account
# rejects it — "not available for the current SKU" — which is why ASR is
# Deepgram. Verified against the live API on 2026-09-05.

# ── Tokens are minted per join, not configured ──────────────────────────────
# src/app/api/agent/route.ts signs an AccessToken2 for each agent uid and for
# the candidate, using the App Certificate above. There is nothing to paste.
#
# With a certificate enabled on the project and no token, Agora accepts the
# join, reports RUNNING, and the agent dies about a second later with
# "agent exits with reason: RTC connection error". That failure mode cost an
# evening once; it is written down so it cannot cost another.
